Labcat ships the upstream browser runtime without modifying its bytes.
The application integration and sandbox wrapper are separate files.

The corresponding source and build resources supplied by the upstream release
are included in SOURCE.tar.gz, with a complete member/hash manifest in
SOURCE-MANIFEST.json. Both files ship beside the runtime in:

  Repository: frontend/public/structure-viewer/vendor/
  Installed Python package and Docker image:
    labcat/static/structure-viewer/vendor/

SOURCE.tar.gz preserves the complete jmol-16.4.23/src, tools, jars and manifest
trees, source build instructions, copyright/license/changelog, Java2Script
compiler resources, unminified browser wrappers, jQuery source and JavaScript
support-class resources. It excludes demonstration-site data outside src,
prebuilt application JARs and duplicate browser-runtime ZIP archives.
This is a source-distribution subset, not a modified JSmol library. Internal
library resources within src are retained; they are not research output data.

